#!/bin/bash
# End-to-end name eval (learn from a correction → apply on later dictations).
# Offline and deterministic: replays corpus.json (real Parakeet output,
# regenerated by gen.sh) through the app's pure units + Glue.swift.
#   scripts/name-eval/run.sh                 baseline (3504715) and current working tree, side by side
#   scripts/name-eval/run.sh --rev 3504715   one revision (pure files from git; GlueBaseline.swift)
#   scripts/name-eval/run.sh --rev WORKTREE  the working tree only (Glue.swift)
#   -v                                       list every learn decision and every miss
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY=… adds the decision-model modes (never read from the Keychain).
set -uo pipefail
HERE="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)"
W="$(cd "$HERE/../.." && pwd)"
BASE=3504715
PURE="SoundCode SpellingRule CandidateFinder VocabularyResolver EditDiff CorrectionWatchPolicy
RedictationLearner DecisionTypes DecisionClient VocabularyCardQueue VocabularyCacheData FillerRules
RuleLearning VocabularyPipeline"
# Pure files added later (e.g. glue moved out of VocabularyLearning) can be listed here:
PURE="$PURE ${EXTRA_PURE:-}"

REV=""; VERBOSE=""
while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
  case "$1" in
    --rev) REV="$2"; shift 2 ;;
    -v) VERBOSE="-v"; shift ;;
    *) echo "unknown argument: $1" >&2; exit 2 ;;
  esac
done

TMP=$(mktemp -d)
trap 'rm -rf "$TMP"' EXIT

# build <rev|WORKTREE> → prints the binary path; returns non-zero on compile failure.
build() {
  local rev="$1" dir="$TMP/$1" glue
  mkdir -p "$dir"
  for f in $PURE; do
    if [ "$rev" = WORKTREE ]; then
      [ -f "$W/Airboard/$f.swift" ] && cp "$W/Airboard/$f.swift" "$dir/"
    else
      git -C "$W" show "$rev:Airboard/$f.swift" > "$dir/$f.swift" 2>/dev/null || rm -f "$dir/$f.swift"
    fi
  done
  if [ "$rev" != WORKTREE ] && [ "$(git -C "$W" rev-parse --short=7 "$rev" 2>/dev/null)" = "$BASE" ]; then
    glue="$HERE/GlueBaseline.swift"
  else
    glue="$HERE/Glue.swift"
  fi
  if ! swiftc -O -parse-as-library "$dir"/*.swift "$glue" "$HERE/main.swift" -o "$dir/name-eval" > "$dir/compile.log" 2>&1; then
    return 1
  fi
  echo "$dir/name-eval"
}

run_one() {  # rev label
  local bin
  if ! bin=$(build "$1"); then
    echo "!! name-eval [$2]: the sources at $1 do not compile with $( [ "$1" = WORKTREE ] && echo Glue.swift || echo the glue file ):" >&2
    sed -n '1,30p' "$TMP/$1/compile.log" >&2
    echo "!! (expected while other agents are mid-edit; update Glue.swift if VocabularyLearning's glue changed)" >&2
    return 1
  fi
  "$bin" "$HERE/corpus.json" $VERBOSE --label "$2" --summary "$TMP/$2.summary"
}

if [ -n "$REV" ]; then
  if [ "$REV" = WORKTREE ]; then run_one WORKTREE current; else run_one "$REV" "$REV"; fi
  exit $?
fi

run_one "$BASE" baseline
echo
echo "================================================================"
run_one WORKTREE current
ok=$?
echo
echo "================ baseline ($BASE) vs current (working tree) ================"
if [ $ok -eq 0 ]; then
  awk -F'\t' 'NR==FNR { b[$1]=$2; order[++n]=$1; next } { c[$1]=$2 }
    END { printf "%-42s %10s %10s\n", "metric", "baseline", "current";
          for (i=1;i<=n;i++) { k=order[i]; printf "%-42s %10s %10s\n", k, b[k], (k in c ? c[k] : "n/a") } }' \
    "$TMP/baseline.summary" "$TMP/current.summary"
else
  echo "current: DID NOT COMPILE (see error above) — baseline printed only"
  awk -F'\t' '{ printf "%-42s %10s\n", $1, $2 }' "$TMP/baseline.summary"
fi
